    id: "L25",
    number: 25,
    week: 9,
    moduleId: "m9",
    title: "PortSwigger Web Academy: SQL Injection - 3 labs",
    description: `Complete three PortSwigger Web Academy SQL injection labs that build on each other in difficulty — bypassing a WHERE clause to see hidden data, a UNION attack to exfiltrate arbitrary table data, and blind SQLi where there is no visible output at all and success must be inferred from a true/false response difference.`,
    platform: "PortSwigger",
    difficulty: "medium",
    estimatedHours: 4,
    instructions: [
      `Open 'SQL injection vulnerability in WHERE clause allowing retrieval of hidden data' at portswigger.net/web-security/sql-injection/lab-retrieve-hidden-data`,
      `Send the category filter request to Repeater and inject category=Gifts' OR 1=1-- - to bypass the released=1 condition and reveal unreleased products`,
      `Open 'SQL injection UNION attack, determining the number of columns returned by the query' at .../sql-injection/union-attacks/lab-determine-number-of-columns`,
      `Use ORDER BY 1, ORDER BY 2, etc. (or UNION SELECT NULL,NULL,...) incrementally until you find the exact column count without an error`,
      `Extend to a full UNION SELECT username, password FROM users-- - payload once the column count and text-compatible columns are known, to dump credentials`,
      `Open 'Blind SQL injection with conditional responses' at .../sql-injection/blind/lab-conditional-responses`,
      `Confirm the injection point by comparing responses to TrackingId cookie payloads that evaluate to true vs false (e.g. ' AND '1'='1 vs ' AND '1'='2)`,
      `Use Burp Intruder with a Simple-list payload of characters and a Grep-Match on the true-condition response to extract the administrator password one character at a time via SUBSTRING`,
      `Log in as administrator with the recovered password to confirm the blind SQLi lab is solved`,
      `Screenshot the green completion banner for all 3 labs`,
    ],
    resources: [
      {
        title:
          "Lab: SQL injection vulnerability in WHERE clause allowing retrieval of hidden data",
        url: "https://portswigger.net/web-security/sql-injection/lab-retrieve-hidden-data",
        type: "platform",
