              payload: "carlos's transcript, including his password",
            },
          ],
        },
      },
      {
        title: "Find the hidden admin panel via robots.txt",
        body: "Appending /robots.txt to the lab's base URL discloses a Disallow: entry pointing at the hidden admin panel path; navigating straight to that path without ever logging in as an administrator reaches the panel, and its exposed 'Delete user' action removes carlos to solve the lab.",
        diagram: {
          type: "browser-mockup",
          url: "/robots.txt",
          annotations: [
            {
              label: "Disallow: entry",
              note: "discloses the admin panel's real path",
            },
            {
              label: "Admin panel",
              note: "reachable directly, no login required -- 'Delete user' removes carlos",
            },
          ],
        },
      },
      {
        title: "Same root cause, two shapes",
        body: "Both labs solve the same underlying flaw -- authorization enforced only by obscurity (a guessable ID, an unlisted URL) rather than a real server-side check -- which is why hiding an admin panel's link in the UI or in robots.txt is not the same as protecting it.",
      },
    ],
