    title: "PortSwigger: File Upload Attacks - 2 labs",
    description: `Bypass an extension blacklist and a Content-Type header check on two PortSwigger Web Academy File Upload labs to get a working PHP web shell onto the server, then use it to exfiltrate a protected file -- the practical skill behind almost every unrestricted-upload finding in a real bug bounty.`,
